-- Fixture for `l4 export dmn`'s empty-model refusal (smucclaw/l4-ide#1104).
--
-- The module has one MEANS and one DECIDE, and the population filter (spec
-- §2.5.6) leaves both out: `sample prices` is referenced only from the
-- #ASSERT, and `price with tax` only from that test scaffolding. The refusal
-- must say so, name both, and point at --include-tests, which puts them back;
-- it must not say the module has no DECIDE or MEANS.

IMPORT prelude

`sample prices` MEANS LIST 10, 20

GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `price with tax` p IS p TIMES 1.1

#ASSERT count (map `price with tax` `sample prices`) EQUALS 2
